# Files written by scripts/build-glossary-bundle.cjs on every build.
#
# The generator always writes LF. Without pinning, core.autocrlf=true checks them out as CRLF on
# Windows, so every local `npm run build` leaves a phantom modification — git reports the file as
# modified while `git diff` prints nothing and the byte counts match exactly.
#
# It is harmless in itself, and that is the problem: it trains you to ignore a dirty working tree
# after a build, which is precisely the habit that lets a real change go unnoticed. The build is
# byte-deterministic by design; pinning the line endings is what keeps "a clean build produces no
# diff" actually true.
glossary/MISUSE.md                         text eol=lf
glossary/QUARANTINE.md                     text eol=lf
glossary/candidates/pending.json           text eol=lf
web/library/glossary/glossary-bundle.json  text eol=lf
